        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for your time making this. As I explained in #671, this is not planned to contain complexity of tag textobject.\r\n\r\n> It seems like this [test](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/1cd8d7e8318071eddc536815f5cafe50b012ac29/tests/test_ai.lua?plain=1#L2558) is failing. Any ideas on how to re-adjust the pattern to satisfy an empty tag name as well?\r\n\r\nI think using this definition would have worked:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\n  ['t'] = { '<(%w-)%f[^<%w][^<>]->.-</%1>', { '^<>().*()</>$', '^<.-[^=]>().*()</[^/]->$' } },\r\n```",
            "created_at": "2024-01-26T10:10:21Z",
